v2 changelog
============

Running log of every change made toward v2 (the soldier-swarm
rebuild). One entry per change. WHAT + WHY, kept short.

Plan of record: port.md
Lessons from v1:    lessons.md

When v2 moves to its own repo, this file moves with it as the
seed of that repo's CHANGELOG / dev_log.

---

2026-05-13  Nail #10: build costs (drain side)
  WHAT: Buildings now consume currencies on construction.
        Per (line, tier) cost table in costs.ts. Thematic
        costs: settlement→wood, farmland→pop+wood,
        forestry→pop, mining→pop+wood, merchant→gold+wood.
        Growth roughly 3x per tier so each upgrade is a
        real decision. Tier cards now show cost, gate the
        "available" state on affordability, and a new
        "unaffordable" CSS state (muted amber, "need 18
        more wood") sits between locked and available.
        Spawn now seeds 30 pop + 30 wood per nation so the
        player can immediately afford a tier-1 building.
  WHY:  Without costs, the player could max every line
        everywhere — no prioritization. Costs activate the
        trade-off layer: do I spend my wood on a settlement
        for more pop, or save it for a forestry mill?
        Also: tile-resource competition (forests vs ore vs
        farmland) now bites economically, not just for the
        line-locking rule.

  Architecture:
   - costs.ts (NEW): single COSTS[line][tier] table;
     canAfford(econ, line, tier), payCost(econ, line, tier),
     formatCost(line, tier), shortfallText(econ, ...).
     Tuning surface = the table.
   - main.ts spawnNations: economy seeded with 30 pop +
     30 wood (was emptyEconomy()).
   - main.ts onBuild: order is now validate → buildTier
     (which checks tier == cur+1) → payCost. Failing
     buildTier means we don't deduct.
   - stateMenu.ts: tier cards gained a cost line ("cost:
     30 wood, 15 pop"). renderTiers now branches into 5
     mutually-exclusive states: built / locked-by-resource
     / locked-by-prev-tier / unaffordable / available.
     Tap target only on available.
   - CSS: new .state-menu-tier.unaffordable (muted amber)
     so the player sees "almost ready" rather than "out of
     reach" — different shade from .locked.

  Notes for future:
   - No maintenance costs. Buildings cost once, produce
     forever. Future polish: per-tick upkeep per building
     (food for pop, wood for buildings, etc).
   - No refund on demolish. There's no demolish UI yet.
   - AI still doesn't build, so they can't spend either.
     "AI builds too" is now the obvious next nail — and
     the same cost table will gate AI builds the same way.

