2026-05-13  Nail #9: production effects
  WHAT: Built tiers now actually output resources per second.
        Five currencies, one per building line: pop / food /
        wood / ore / gold. Per-tier base rates 1 / 3 / 7 u/s.
        Matching line on matching state gets a 2x boost (the
        ★ finally pays off). Settlement is universal (no
        matching boost — it doesn't have a resource match by
        design) but always produces pop. Per-nation
        accumulator on Nation.economy; readout shows the
        player's five totals as one new line.
  WHY:  User picked it: "Production effects (the big
        foundational one)." Was the lynchpin that made
        everything else (costs, AI economy, victory) sit on
        air. Now the build menu and the resource-matching
        rule both have a payoff the player can SEE.

  Architecture:
   - economy.ts (NEW): Currency type, Economy struct,
     emptyEconomy, currencyForLine, productionRate(line,
     tier, isMatching), currencyLabel. Single source of
     truth for the rate table. Tuning is two constants:
     BASE_RATE_PER_TIER and MATCH_BOOST.
   - nation.ts: Nation gains `economy: Economy`. Initialized
     to all-zeros in spawnNations.
   - main.ts: tickProduction(dtMs) per frame — for each
     alive nation, for each owned state, for each built
     building, add rate * dt to the matching currency.
     O(states * lines) per tick = ~750 ops, negligible.
   - readout: one new "econ: pop X · food X · wood X ·
     ore X · gold X" line under the recruit line.

  Notes for future:
   - No costs yet. Buildings still free + instant. Costs
     are the next natural nail — they consume from
     nation.economy, gating the build menu.
   - No spending. Resources only accumulate. When costs
     and unit upgrades land, the accumulator drains.
   - No cap. Numbers grow unbounded. Probably fine for
     now; a population cap (food gating pop growth)
     comes naturally with food costs.
   - AIs have 0 economy — they don't build. The gap will
     widen until "AI builds too" lands (depends on this
     nail being in first).

