2026-05-11  Movement model: STRAIGHT LINE or reject
  WHAT: Reverted the BFS auto-routing from the previous
        commit. Drag-to-move is now literally a straight
        line. Drop validation samples along the line; if any
        sample sits in another nation's territory (other
        than the destination region itself), the entire
        drop is rejected — the army doesn't go partway, and
        it doesn't route around the obstacle.
  WHY:  User's feedback after trying the BFS version:
        "if I draw a straight line the army should move
        straight. If the army can't move the full line
        don't allow any movement. Right now it's making
        right angles when I drew straight lines."
        The right-angles came from BFS routing through
        region centroids. Straight-line is what was asked
        for from the start; I misread "path doesn't go
        through enemy land" as "find a path that doesn't,"
        not "the line you drew is the path."

  Architecture:
   - army.ts: ArmyDeps.pathfind → canMoveTo(fromX, fromY,
     toX, toY) boolean. endDrag calls it before committing
     a single-waypoint march. False = reject, previous
     march resumes.
   - main.ts: pathfindForNation replaced with
     canNationMoveStraight. Samples at TILE_SIZE/2 along
     the straight line; rejects on any non-destination
     enemy region touched.
   - Waypoint queue infra in army.ts stays (cheap, future-
     friendly), but now always single-waypoint per drop.

