2026-05-11  Mid-game land grab: enemy non-capital regions
  WHAT: Enemy non-capital regions can now be taken without
        capturing the enemy's capital. Mechanic: stand your
        army in an enemy region (not marching) with no enemy
        army within COMBAT_TRIGGER_RADIUS for REGION_HOLD_MS
        (5s) and the region flips. Combat naturally resets
        the hold timer (enemy in range cancels capture).
        Symmetric for AIs — they take your regions the same
        way. Also bumped CAPITAL_HOLD_MS from 15s to 10s per
        user's tuning.
  WHY:  Pre-existing rule "enemy regions only flip via
        capital capture" made the gameplay binary — you
        either nibbled neutrals or went all-in on the
        capital. No mid-game friction. The hold-based take
        gives you a real middle stage: weaken the enemy by
        capturing border regions, watch their cap shrink,
        then go for the capital. AIs do the same to you, so
        ignoring your borders is no longer free.

  Architecture:
   - nation.ts: regionCaptureProgress field (parallel to
     captureProgress but for individual regions)
   - main.ts: REGION_HOLD_MS = 5_000; CAPITAL_HOLD_MS dropped
     to 10_000
   - main.ts: tickRegionClaims extended — neutral instant
     claim retained; enemy non-capital regions now start a
     hold-capture timer. Capitals still routed through
     tickCapture (NOT here) so the cascade-flip on capital
     capture is preserved.
   - readout: "capturing region #X (Ys)" / "region #X under
     siege by #N (Ys)" lines, appended after the main
     status line.

  Notes for future:
   - AI doesn't currently prioritize defending its own
     regions under siege. pickExpansionTarget prefers
     neutrals; only after neutrals exhausted do AIs grab
     enemy land. Region-defense AI is a polish nail.
   - No visual capture-ring on the region itself yet (just
     readout text). Polish later.

