2026-05-11  Nail #6.4: recruitment + extensible upgrade hooks
  WHAT: Capitals now generate soldiers over time. Each owned
        capital adds +1 unit-time/sec to your nation's
        recruitment rate. Player picks the unit type via a
        "recruit: INF/CAV" toggle button in the top-right.
        Infantry costs 1 unit-time per soldier (so 1 inf/sec
        at one capital), cavalry costs 2 unit-time (1 cav per
        2s). AIs recruit too — they default to infantry. Army
        cap scales with territory: 50 base + 10 per owned
        region, so expansion enables a bigger army.
        Recruitment pauses at cap, resumes after casualties.
        Wiped armies are no longer destroyed — the Army
        instance hangs around invisible, and the first
        recruited soldier respawns the army at the capital.
        Defeat condition relaxed to "capital captured only"
        (was: capital OR army). Losing your army is now
        recoverable as long as you hold home.
  WHY:  Without recruitment, every casualty was permanent and
        the game got steeper as it went. With recruitment, a
        bad battle can be recovered from — strategic depth
        comes from defending your capital long enough for
        production to refill your army. The unit-cost system
        ("time proportional to strength") gives the player a
        real choice each map: cheap fast inf vs slow strong
        cav. The recruitment-rate function is the planned
        extension point for buildings/upgrades the user
        flagged in the big-picture note — currently it's just
        `capitals × 1`, but the shape is a single function
        call that future systems can multiply / add into.

  Architecture:
   - units.ts: recruitCost on UnitDef (inf 1, cav 2)
   - nation.ts: recruitmentPick + recruitmentProgress fields
   - army.ts: new respawnAt(x, y) — resets position to capital
     when an empty army is being rebuilt
   - main.ts: getRecruitmentRate(n), getArmyCap(n),
     totalSoldierCount(n), addSoldier(n, type), tickRecruitment
   - main.ts: removed army.destroy() on battle wipe — Armies
     persist hidden until recruitment refills them.
     captureCapital is the only path that genuinely tears
     down an Army.
   - main.ts: defeat condition simplified to capital-captured.
   - index.html: #recruit-toggle button (top-right under
     "new map"); same min-height 44px for phone tappability.
   - readout: new "recruit: TYPE X% · current/cap · rate/s"
     line. Falls back to "AT CAP" or "no capital" wording
     when recruitment isn't progressing.
   - Per-frame readout render (replacing throttle) so the
     recruitment % ticks visibly.

  Tuning constants:
   - RECRUIT_RATE_PER_CAPITAL = 1 (unit-time / sec / capital)
   - ARMY_CAP_BASE = 50
   - ARMY_CAP_PER_REGION = 10
   - UNIT_DEFS.infantry.recruitCost = 1
   - UNIT_DEFS.cavalry.recruitCost = 2

  Notes for future nails:
   - Building/upgrade nail: extend getRecruitmentRate(n) to
     read per-capital buildings. Same hook for resource
     yield.
   - Resource cost: introduce a "gold" pool on Nation;
     gate addSoldier on gold >= unit.goldCost. Same shape
     as time-cost gate today.

