2026-05-09  Nail #6.3 (overnight): full gameplay loop
  WHAT: Game is now playable end-to-end in a single session.
        Three nations on every map (1 player + 2 AIs), each
        with a starting capital, a randomized regiment army,
        and a color. AIs expand to neutral neighbor regions
        every ~10s (jittered), fight each other silently when
        their armies meet (Simulate runs behind the scenes
        with a brief crossed-swords icon flashing at the
        engagement point). Player engages AIs the same way as
        #6.2 — drag-march into them and the action menu opens.
        Battles still resolve through the existing Simulate
        path. New: capital occupation. Standing within 24
        world-units of a non-owned capital starts a 15-second
        hold timer; finishing the hold flips that region (and
        all the eliminated nation's other regions) to the
        captor's color, and the eliminated nation's army is
        removed from the map. Symmetric: AIs do the same to
        the player. When an AI's capital is being besieged,
        the AI re-routes their army to defend ("fight back"
        per user spec). Win = capture all enemy capitals.
        Defeat = your army destroyed OR your capital captured.
        Either triggers a modal overlay with the appropriate
        label and a NEW MAP button.
  WHY:  Closes the gameplay loop. After #6.2 the game was a
        beautiful battle scaffolding with no progression —
        one fight and you were done. Now each map is a real
        session with stakes, expansion pressure, and a clean
        win/lose state. Aligns with port.md milestone 1
        spec: 3 players, capture-capitals win condition,
        no-recruitment-yet OK.

  Big-picture design: introduced a first-class Nation type
        (color, capitalRegionId, capital tile coord, army,
        isPlayer flag, eliminated, capture timer). Region
        ownership is a separate Int16Array indexed by region
        id — explicit, mutable, rebuildable. Capital tile is
        a real coordinate, not an inferred concept. This
        scaffolds the future systems the user flagged:
        resources/economy/upgrades all attach to Nation, and
        regions are first-class possessions with intrinsic
        value (not just battle tokens).

  Module map:
   - nation.ts (new) — Nation interface
   - gameModal.ts (new) — VICTORY/DEFEAT modal overlay
   - mapRender.ts — rewrite. Ownership-aware tints + capital
        markers. New rebuildOwnerLayers() called on region
        flip events.
   - army.ts — ArmyDeps gained homeRegionId + color; new
        marchTo(x,y) and isMarching() for programmatic AI use.
   - main.ts — major rewrite. Replaces enemy/army singletons
        with nations[] array. Symmetric capture state per
        Nation. AI expansion tick. AI vs AI silent battles.
        Win/defeat detection wired to all the right entry
        points (battle exit, capture completion, army loss).
   - index.html — game-modal markup + CSS.

  Tuning constants (battle for these in main.ts):
   - AI_NATION_COUNT = 2 (port.md M1: 3 players total)
   - AI_DECIDE_INTERVAL_MS = 10_000 (±2.5s jitter)
   - CAPITAL_HOLD_MS = 15_000
   - CAPITAL_HOLD_RADIUS = 24 world units
   - SIEGE_RESPONSE_INTERVAL_MS = 2_000 (how often a besieged
        AI re-issues a "march home" order)
   - AI_BATTLE_ICON_MS = 1200

