2026-05-09  #6.2 follow-up #2: rounds sim + commitment + cooldown
  WHAT: Rewrote Simulate's combat resolver as a rounds-based
        loop using real per-soldier stats (atk, def, hp on
        infantry and cavalry). Each round, both sides exchange
        damage simultaneously; after every round each side
        checks two retreat conditions (force ratio < 0.4 OR
        casualties > 60% of starting power). First side to
        either condition retreats; both at once → mutual rout.
        Result panel now shows the outcome label ("ENEMY
        ROUTED" / "PLAYER ROUTED" / "MUTUAL ROUT" / "ENEMY
        ANNIHILATED" / "PLAYER ANNIHILATED"). Once the player
        touches the enemy they are committed — the old
        "drag away during 500ms pre-roll cancels battle" path
        is gone. Army movement is frozen from the moment of
        contact through the entire battle scene. After the
        exit transition, the engagement enters a 5-second
        cooldown; touching the enemy again does nothing until
        the timer expires (readout shows "regrouping...").
  WHY:  The old single-shot head-count comparison gave both
        sides equal hits and felt arbitrary. Real stats +
        rounds gives the simulation the "fight until one side
        breaks" feel the user asked for, and lets unit type
        composition matter (cavalry: heavier hitter, no armor;
        infantry: balanced + armored). Commitment + cooldown
        close the loophole where you could either chicken out
        before pre-roll completed, or instantly re-attack the
        same enemy after a loss. With the cooldown the loser
        gets breathing room to either retreat physically or
        accept they can't take this region.

  Implementation: units.ts grew atk/def/hp fields on UnitDef.
        battleSim.ts rewritten: per-round simultaneous damage
        with hp-share distribution and per-regiment armor
        reduction (DAMAGE_SCALE=0.5, DEF_SCALE=0.3, capped at
        MAX_ROUNDS=30 as a stalemate guard). New SimOutcome
        union; old SimResult shape preserved + outcome and
        rounds added. battleMenu.ts maps outcome to a header
        label, otherwise unchanged. main.ts simplified
        CombatState from idle|engaged|retreating to
        idle|engaged|cooldown; engagement detection gated on
        idle; cooldown ticks back to idle in the ticker;
        zoom/drag lock keyed off `combatState === 'engaged'`
        which now covers both pre-roll and in-battle. Battle
        exit transition completion sets the cooldown timer.

  Tuning notes (in case it feels off):
   - 50 inf vs 50 inf → ~5 rounds, mutual rout
   - 50+20 vs 50+20 (mixed) → ~4 rounds, mutual rout
   - 70 inf vs 50 inf → ~2 rounds, enemy routed
   - Single units / glass cannons → cavalry gets minced fast
     unless paired with infantry to absorb hits

